.el .ds Aq '
.TH taurctl-key 1  "taurctl-key " 
.SH NAME
taurctl\-key \- Manage SSH public keys used for git pushes over SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaurctl key\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage SSH public keys used for git pushes over SSH
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Server URL (overrides TAUR_SERVER and the config file)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Config directory (default: $TAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print raw JSON
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin instead of prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
taurctl\-key\-list(1)
List your SSH keys
.TP
taurctl\-key\-add(1)
Add a public key from a file (e.g. ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub) or `\-` for stdin
.TP
taurctl\-key\-remove(1)
Remove a key by id
.TP
taurctl\-key\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
